00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.110
episode

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.150
"Adieu, My Youth"

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.650
Is it true she escaped from prison?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.690
What a feat. Just what you'd
expect from Jeanne.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.900
The one who helped her escape...
Maybe it was the Queen?

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.800
No way.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.540
No, it's got to be her!

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.570
She made Jeanne take all the blame
in the necklace incident,

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.110
so I bet even the Queen had
to clear her conscience.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:14.450
Rumor has it that it was the nobles who resent
the royal family that helped her escape though.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.260
That's because everyone knows about
the quarreling factions inside Versailles.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.180
<i>Sister...</i>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.590
<i>Where are you, Jeanne?</i>

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.330
<i>No...</i>

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.090
<i>Where you are doesn't matter...</i>

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.510
<i>As long as it's a place...</i>

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.470
<i>...where you can be yourself and fly freely.</i>

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.830
Madame Polignac!

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.850
It's been a while, Mademoiselle Rosalie.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.350
The last time we saw each other was
when Charlotte died, wasn't it?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.390
You seem well.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.200
I'm glad.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.790
Please leave.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.850
I've come to see you as your mother today.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.660
Please stop!

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.750
I don't consider you my mother.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.840
You still hate me, don't you?

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.120
And rightly so.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.030
That the woman who raised you,
Nicole Lamorlière{Moliàre},

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.490
died was my fault, even though it was an accident.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.470
Still, I'm your birth mother.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.730
That'll never change.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.420
I'm just beginning to forget my hatred for you.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:10.650
It also means I'm trying to forget
that you gave birth to me, as well.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:14.540
So please... don't ever
show yourself to me again.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.500
Don't say such sad things, Rosalie.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.800
Please... come to the Polignac manor.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.540
Ever since Charlotte died, I'm all alone.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.090
I want you to live with me.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.010
That won't happen.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.950
Hey, did you hear that fugitive
Jeanne published a book?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:43.860
A book?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.460
It's one of those secret publications where the author's
and publisher's whereabouts are a mystery.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.890
Really? Gutsy move!

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.960
It basically proved that Jeanne has
a bigwig supporter behind her.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.040
That means the military and provost will never
catch her, no matter how hard they try.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.190
Good for her!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.250
Come on, have a read!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.740
''The Memoirs of Jeanne Valois!''

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.650
The first volume has all the details on
\hthe truth behind the necklace incident!

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.180
And that's not all!

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.320
The second and third volumes will
be published soon, as well!

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.690
But before that, you need
to read the first volume!

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.120
Here. Thank you for your purchase.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.310
Here you go. Thank you.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.270
''The Memoirs of Jeanne Valois, Volume 1 .''

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.740
''Tales on the Scandal of Marie Antoinette,
Chapter 1 : A Catalog of the Queen's Lovers.''

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.550
Yeah, you're in here.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.660
''A Fair Lady in Men's Attire:
Colonel Oscar François de Jarjayes.''

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.290
You're listed right after Madame Polignac.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.090
Jeanne Valois...

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.240
She sure is something.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.200
Rosalie?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.530
I'm so sorry, Lady Oscar!

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.940
I couldn't care less what it says about me.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.710
I'm more concerned about the mentality of
the people that would believe such rubbish,

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:52.680
and how they will view the royal family
and Lady Marie Antoinette as a result.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.640
We must do something about it at once!

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.910
Even with a heavy-handed crackdown,

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.390
the books are still being bought and sold, in bars,
back alleyways and even underground passageways!

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:02.450
Minister of Security!

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.570
You went as far as mobilizing the military to catch one fugitive, yet why haven't you caught her already?!

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.960
It's hard to say.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.300
As you very well know,
when it comes to Jeanne,

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.530
the commoners clam up and refuse
to provide us with any information.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.500
We have no choice. We must ask the royal
household to lend us their resources.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.460
What are you suggesting?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.070
We request they mobilize the Royal Guards!

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.740
Listen! This is a clear threat
to the royal household!

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.380
The Royal Guards have a duty to
protect the royal household!

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:29.980
All right.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.080
Vice Minister of State Affairs,

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.650
dispatch this decree to the Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards at once.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.100
Tell her the council has made its decision.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:47.070
Saverne Monastery

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:51.070
It's selling like crazy!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.030
A professional writer would
keel over if they saw this!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:57.540
I never expected you to have
such a knack for writing, Jeanne!

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.480
Settle down, Nicolas.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.540
Stop being so elated over such silly things.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.670
No matter how much money we
make from selling those books,

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.280
don't forget we can't even step
a foot outside this monastery.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:09.090
Well, sure, but that's only
for a little while longer.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.790
Remember what that Monsieur said.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.960
Once things settle down, he said he'd arrange
for us to live in another country together.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.950
Stop being so naïve.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.430
We don't even know who
that ''Monsieur'' is exactly.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.930
Who knows if we can really trust him.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.810
You know...

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.570
I'm sort of growing tired of all this...

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.220
<i>This ring is from Rosalie.</i>

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.290
<i>She said it was a keepsake of your mother.</i>

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:47.850
<i>Rosalie also said, ''I'm plenty happy already,
so I want my sister Jeanne to have it.''</i>

00:08:55.340 --> 00:09:01.010
My Lady, why must you be
sent in search of a fugitive?

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:03.040
It's the council's decision, Nanna.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.480
I have to follow orders.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.020
Also, that fugitive is Rosalie's...

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.280
Her whereabouts are unknown.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:12.370
It's not set in stone that I'll be
the one to apprehend her.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.700
Please be careful.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.130
Easy now... Easy...

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.500
Mademoiselle Rosalie.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.230
A letter came for you earlier.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.670
The sender only wrote her name as ''J.''

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:38.940
I may be a chatterbox, but I haven't
told anyone, not even Lady Oscar.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:48.620
<i>"Rosalie, you should hold on to the ring."</i>

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.590
<i>"After all, I'm living in happiness right now."</i>

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:52.990
<i>"From Saverne."</i>

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:55.060
<i>She's lying!</i>

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.720
<i>She can't be happy!</i>

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.400
<i>I know, because even when we were young,</i>

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.630
<i>I've never seen her laugh from
the bottom of her heart.</i>

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.580
<i>Just once...</i>

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.000
<i>I wish I could see her laugh joyously someday...</i>

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.510
How do you do, Rosalie?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:19.600
Have you changed your mind about coming to
Polignac manor to be by your mother's side?

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.010
I could never consider such a thing.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:23.810
Please excuse me.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:26.680
Wait, Rosalie.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:31.730
You have no choice, but to listen to what I say.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.110
How so...?

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:38.570
If you don't, Oscar François will be arrested
for her involvement in the necklace case.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.170
Firstly, Jeanne's husband, Nicolas,

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:46.200
was a member of the Royal Guards
Regiment, which Colonel Oscar commands.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.210
Secondly, no one in the royal
household has realized this yet,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.290
but Oscar has taken you,
Jeanne's younger sister, in at her manor.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.210
The culprit's husband is her subordinate,

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.620
and the culprit's sister is living at her manor.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.430
Faced with all these facts,
anyone would assume,

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.120
that Colonel Oscar is a
member of Jeanne's gang.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:09.370
If you refuse to call me your mother
and come to the Polignac manor,

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.190
I'll tell the necessary authorities
and make it public!

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.310
Now, Rosalie! Call me your mother!

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.820
Charge!

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.090
Wait, you!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.710
It's not Jeanne.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:49.640
She's just the female ringleader
of a band of thieves.

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.770
We've been fooled by another false lead.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.550
Oscar.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.400
Shouldn't we be glad that it was a false lead?

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.660
Still, long journeys like this, day after day,
are starting to really wear on us...

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.870
On the troops, you and me included.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:32.170
I hear Colonel Oscar was also ordered
to capture Jeanne Valois.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:35.920
Years could go by, but Oscar François
will never catch Jeanne and her gang.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.980
On the contrary, she'd probably
help with her escape.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.890
It's certainly time I informed
the Minister of Security,

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:45.790
that the Regiment Commander of the Royal
Guards is sheltering Jeanne Valois' sister.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:46.730
You can't!

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:47.530
Anything but that!

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.900
The longer it takes Colonel
Oscar to capture Jeanne,

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.960
the more suspicious people will become.

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:56.970
I don't want to burden Lady Oscar
with any more trouble!

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:57.420
Well?

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.040
I'll...

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.980
I'll do as you say...!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:02.890
Mother...

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:04.950
I see.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.450
Such a good girl, Rosalie.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.480
Jeanne has finished writing all the books?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:26.540
Yes, all five volumes of ''The Memoirs
of Jeanne Valois'' are complete.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:28.640
In that case, she's no longer of use.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:29.940
What would you like to do?

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:33.500
If you'd like, I could head
to Saverne tonight and...!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.790
Don't get ahead of yourself!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.940
It isn't necessary for us to do
the dirty work ourselves.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.090
There are plenty of other ways.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.310
Oscar, don't be surprised.
It's Rosalie...

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:06.180
Um... I'd like to say goodbye to Lady Oscar.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.410
Go ahead, but keep it short.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.560
Lady Oscar!

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.460
Thank you for looking after me for so long.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.880
I've decided to go to the Polignac manor.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.660
I wasn't told of this!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:24.530
I wasn't told about any of this!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.840
Why are you leaving so suddenly?!

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.930
I've been thinking about it for a while now.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.800
How I should return to my mother's
side someday...

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.760
Something happened, hasn't it, Rosalie?!

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.720
What happened when I wasn't looking?!

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.470
I must leave now...!

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.100
Rosalie, wait!

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:50.790
All right, I won't ask any more questions.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.310
Madame Polignac is your birth mother.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.660
Promise me you'll find your happiness.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.220
Y-Yes...!

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:30.590
She was such a nice girl...

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.500
She was like a spring breeze...

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.500
<i>Adieu, my youth...</i>

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:39.000
<i>Adieu, my happiness...</i>

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:42.000
<i>Adieu, my Lady Oscar...</i>

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:44.340
Um, My Lady.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:47.610
Mademoiselle Rosalie handed me this earlier.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.520
This letter...!

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:52.510
It's from Jeanne!

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.890
Jeanne is in... Saverne!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.260
<i>Rosalie...</i>

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.160
How she must have felt...

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:07.460
She didn't...

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.560
She didn't have to do this...

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.900
André, don't tell anyone about this!

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.840
Give me some time to think about it.

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:17.250
I understand.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.710
Colonel Oscar François de Jarjayes!

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.250
You have been summoned by
the Minister of Security!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.980
Please come to the Palace of Versailles at once!

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:33.720
A well-connected individual received an
anonymous tip and has just informed us,

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:37.400
that Jeanne Valois is hiding
in a monastery in Saverne.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:40.730
Colonel, take your platoon and head
to Saverne immediately.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.570
Well? Did you agree to take on the mission?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.280
Yeah, I agreed.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.570
Now that Jeanne's whereabouts are known,
if not me, someone else will go regardless.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:01.890
If she's going to be captured either way,
the least I can do is capture her myself...

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.130
That's why I agreed...

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:15.330
It's the Royal Guards platoon,
led by Colonel Oscar.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:17.200
They're on their way to Saverne.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.200
Poor Jeanne.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.340
I'm sure she never expected us to sell her out.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:37.780
Mother Mary, I'm feeling great tonight!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.370
J-Jeanne!

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.090
Come see this!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.640
What is it?

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:52.800
What's the matter?

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.050
Something strange is going on outside!

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.950
I-It's the Royal Guards!

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.430
Damn it, we're surrounded already!

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.350
Jeanne Valois!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.720
Nicolas de la Motte!

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.860
I am Oscar François de Jarjayes!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.610
Surrender peacefully and
no force will be used!

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.360
Come out, Jeanne!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.120
Surrender yourself, Captain la Motte!

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.300
Wh-What do we do, Jeanne?!

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:21.580
We're doomed!

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.100
Pull yourself together and act like a man.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.870
Now that it's come down to this,
what will be will be.

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:32.770
Commander, let's raid the building!

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:35.180
Wait. Not yet.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.600
First, I'll inspect the building alone.

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:41.930
Oscar!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.980
If you hear a gunshot, do not hesitate.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:47.510
Proceed with an all-out attack immediately.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.130
Until then, leave everything to me!

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.560
No one is to interfere!

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.570
That's an order!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.240
Oscar...

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:16.760
Wait, Captain!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.260
A gunshot is the signal for an all-out attack.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.470
If you shoot me, my men will
raid the building immediately.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.800
Now, come with me.

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.100
If you need to change your clothes, I can wait.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.940
This place... was it Rosalie who told you?

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:44.410
It wasn't Rosalie. I assure you.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.720
I see... I'm glad then...

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:53.860
Even someone like me still has an ally...
Just one, but someone I can trust...

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.760
I'm so glad...

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.440
Jeanne, I just had a great idea!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:12.840
Let's use her as a hostage
and make a run for it!

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.780
If you want to run, you're on your own.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:17.180
I don't care anymore...

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:19.690
I've sort of grown tired of it all...

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.180
Wh-What? But that's...!

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:25.020
Fine then!

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.830
In that case...!

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:32.230
I don't need a hostage if I'm escaping alone!

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.750
There's no use in keeping her alive!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.230
André...

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.670
She called for me!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.010
Just now...!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.740
I'm certain Oscar called for me!

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:47.040
Cut it out. I didn't hear a thing.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:48.710
André!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:49.810
We were ordered to stay here!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.850
<i>To Hell with the order!</i>

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:57.650
You...!

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:01.490
Stop!

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:04.430
Killing her isn't going to save us either way.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.070
Never mind that...

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.950
Won't you die with me?

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:19.000
Oscar!

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:20.540
Oscar!

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:21.710
Are you all right, Oscar?!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:22.980
The cellar...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.780
They went down into the cellar...

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:25.850
Jeanne intends to die...!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:29.880
<i>This smell...</i>

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:37.940
It's gunpowder!

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.940
I'm sorry, Nicolas...

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.040
I'm sorry... I'd be lonely
if I died alone.

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:48.310
It's all right...

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:52.200
Besides, you were the best woman I ever met...

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.440
Really?

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:54.280
I'm so happy...

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:14.730
<i>Thus, "The Affair of the Diamond
Necklace" had come to an end.</i>

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:16.970
<i>However, who helped Jeanne
escape from prison...</i>

00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:20.110
<i>...and aided the publishing of her memoir?</i>

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:25.610
<i>It's said that it was the King's cousin, Duke Orléans,
who secretly plotted to steal the throne,</i>

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:31.320
<i>but along with Jeanne's death, the truth
was forever lost in darkness.</i>

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:33.210
To be continued

